            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0389" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.38/123: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-26T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 28,
                            4.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s June 22, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>] p.m. Note delivered
                    yesterday to the President who fully shares in the views therein expressed as to
                    future legislation.</p>
                <pb facs="0390" n="305" xml:id="pg305"/>
                <p>As to the details for the execution of the arrangement in question, the President
                    desires that after discussing the matter and being informed, that these details
                    should be embodied in memoranda etc. Stated that he would prepare a memorandum
                    to that end.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
